※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=7 diag=none

※ Multiplication binds tighter than addition, as it does in writing, and both
※ bind tighter than the bitwise operators: this is (1 ⊞ (2 ⊠ 3)) and so 7.

let one: u6 = 1u6
let two: u6 = 2u6
let three: u6 = 3u6

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    one ⊞ two ⊠ three
